   "text": "Extended tier only"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- An electric field is defined as: **A region of space in which an electric charge experiences a force**\n- The direction of an electric field at a point is defined as: **The direction of the force on a positive charge at that point**\n- Charged objects **create** electric fields around themselves\n\n  - This is similar to how magnets create magnetic fields"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- An electric field is a **vector **quantity as it has both **magnitude **(strength) and **direction**"
  }
 ]
